{
  "$comment": "#NEW-145 / #NEW-143 D2-D3 (Danny 2026-11-26): SKILLS OVER MCP on Exponential's MCP server, the `io.modelcontextprotocol/skills` extension (github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ext-skills specification/beta/skills.mdx; modelcontextprotocol.io/extensions/skills/overview). The server declares `capability` in `server/discover` (resources + the extension with `directoryRead: true`) and implements `skills/list`, `skills/get`, `resources/read` of every served file and `resources/directory/read`. WHAT IS SERVED (`servedSkills`): (1) TEAM SKILLS: every own skill (packages/domain-contract fixtures/skills.json; `builtin` rows excluded) of every team the credential reaches, the teams `resolveTeamAccess` (lib/auth/access.ts) grants it read on (an agent's or a confined token's clamp included), at `skill://<team-slug>/<name>/SKILL.md`, sorted by slug then name (code point); (2) THE BUILT-INS `builtins` (D3: genUI and the Exponential workflow, from packages/exponential-ui/skills, not the apps or Motion skills) at `skill://exponential/<name>/SKILL.md` (`builtinRoot`), in `builtins` order, after the team skills. A team whose slug is `exponential` keeps its own skills under the same root; at a built-in's exact URI the built-in wins and the team skill is not served (`listCases` `shadowed`). A skill of a team the credential does not reach is answered exactly like one that does not exist (`errors.notServed`): no existence leak. BYTES: a built-in serves its shipped files verbatim (SKILL.md, then `files` sorted by path); a team skill serves ONE file, SKILL.md = `teamSkillMd(name, description, body)`: `---\\nname: <name>\\ndescription: <JSON string>\\n---\\n\\n<body trimmed>\\n`. FRONTMATTER in a listing = exactly {name, description}, never `allowed-tools` or any other key, whatever a body says (a body's own `---` block is body text). MANIFEST (`resources`) is COMPLETE: every served file of the skill, SKILL.md FIRST, each {uri, digest, size}: `digest` = `sha256:` + the lowercase hex SHA-256 of exactly the bytes `resources/read` returns (UTF-8), `size` = their byte length (`digestCases`; `specExamples.codeReview` replays the overview's example byte for byte; `specExamples.gitWorkflow` is the spec's listing entry, whose body is unpublished, kept for its shape). Never `\"dynamic\"`. CACHE HINTS on every result: `ttlMs` = 300000; `cacheScope` = `private` for a team skill (its get, its reads, and any listing carrying one) and `public` for a built-in (and a listing of built-ins only). `skills/list` is ONE page: a `cursor` is refused. `skills/get {uri}` takes a SKILL.md URI only. `resources/read` returns {uri, mimeType (`mimeTypes` by extension), text}. `resources/directory/read` (D: `directoryRead`) lists the DIRECT children of a skill directory (the skill root `skill://<root>/<name>` or a folder under it): SKILL.md first, then by name; a folder = `directoryMimeType`; a team skill's root lists its SKILL.md only. ERRORS (JSON-RPC `errorCode` -32602, `errors`, `errorCases`): a missing or non-string uri (`missingUri`), a URI that is malformed, unknown, of an unreached team, or not a file (`notServed`), a directory read of a file (`notDirectory`), a cursor (`badCursor`). A URI is `scheme` + root + `/` + name + optional `/path`; root and name match `segmentPattern`; no query, fragment, backslash, NUL, empty, `.` or `..` segment, trailing slash, or more than `uriMax` chars (`uriCases`). LIMITS (`limits`, the spec's): at most 512 files and 16 MiB per skill; the shipped built-ins are tested against them.",
  "extension": "io.modelcontextprotocol/skills",
  "capability": {
    "resources": {},
    "extensions": {
      "io.modelcontextprotocol/skills": {
        "directoryRead": true
      }
    }
  },
  "scheme": "skill://",
  "builtinRoot": "exponential",
  "builtins": [
    "exponential-genui",
    "exponential-workflow"
  ],
  "segmentPattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*$",
  "uriMax": 1024,
  "ttlMs": 300000,
  "cacheScope": {
    "team": "private",
    "builtin": "public"
  },
  "mimeTypes": {
    ".md": "text/markdown",
    ".json": "application/json",
    "default": "text/plain"
  },
  "directoryMimeType": "inode/directory",
  "limits": {
    "maxFiles": 512,
    "maxBytes": 16777216
  },
  "errorCode": -32602,
  "errors": {
    "missingUri": "skills: a uri is required.",
    "notServed": "No skill is served at {uri}",
    "notDirectory": "{uri} is not a directory resource",
    "badCursor": "skills/list has one page: no cursor."
  },
  "specExamples": {
